%I A051759 #23 Nov 12 2026 20:53:07
%S A051759 1,2,4,31,307,2,9,755,39302,2652241,59,13697
%N A051759 Consider the problem of placing A051756(n) queens on an n X n board so that each queen attacks precisely 3 others. Sequence gives number of solutions up to square symmetry.
%C A051759 A queen attacks another queen if both are on the same row, column or diagonal and no other queen is between them. If N queens each attack exactly 3 others, then 3*N = 8*N - 2*E, where E is the number of lines (rows, columns and diagonals in both directions, 6*n-2 in all) that contain a queen, since a line containing j queens accounts for 2*(j-1) attacks and each queen lies on 4 lines. So N = 2*E/5 <= 2*floor((6*n-2)/5), the bound in A051756, and when N attains this bound (verified for n <= 100, see A051756) exactly s = (6*n-2) mod 5 lines are empty in every solution. As n increases, s cycles through 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, which accounts for the irregular growth of this sequence. When s = 0 (n == 2 (mod 5)), every line contains a queen, including the four one-cell diagonals at the corners, and a(n) is small (a(7) = 2, a(12) = 59). - _Jeff Sponaugle_, Nov 07 2026
%D A051759 M. Gardner, The Last Recreations, Springer, 1997, p. 282.
%D A051759 M. Gardner, The Colossal Book of Mathematics, 2001, p. 209.
%H A051759 Erich Friedman, <a href="/A051759/a051759.gif">Illustration of initial terms</a>
%H A051759 Sean A. Irvine, <a href="https://github.com/archmageirvine/joeis/blob/master/src/irvine/oeis/a051/A051759.java">Java program</a> (github)
%e A051759 a(3) = 2: the two solutions with A051756(3) = 6 queens on a 3 X 3 board are
%e A051759   Q Q Q   Q Q Q
%e A051759   Q . .   . . .
%e A051759   Q . Q   Q Q Q
%e A051759 In each, exactly (6*3-2) mod 5 = 1 of the 16 lines is empty: an antidiagonal in the first, the middle row in the second.
%e A051759 a(7) = 2: the two solutions with A051756(7) = 16 queens on a 7 X 7 board are
%e A051759   Q Q Q . Q . Q   Q Q Q . . Q Q
%e A051759   . . . . . . Q   . . . Q . . .
%e A051759   . . . Q . . .   . . . . . . Q
%e A051759   Q . . . . . Q   Q . . . . . Q
%e A051759   . . . Q . . .   Q . . . . . .
%e A051759   Q . . . . . .   . . . Q . . .
%e A051759   Q . Q . Q Q Q   Q Q . . Q Q Q
%e A051759 Here (6*7-2) mod 5 = 0, so every row, column and diagonal contains a queen.
%Y A051759 Cf. A051754-A051758, A051567-A051571, A019654.
%K A051759 nonn,nice,more,hard,changed
%O A051759 2,2
